{"name":"Marina Bay Sands","hex":"#d3af37","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"marina","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A harbour for small boats."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/marina"},{"term":"bay","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Batuley."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A body of water (especially the sea) contained by a concave shoreline.","A bank or dam to keep back water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bay"},{"term":"sands","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of sand","sand grains, especially in reference to the contents of an hourglass, from which"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of sand"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sands"}],"entries":[{"title":"Marina Bay Sands","blocks":[{"text":"Marina Bay Sands is an integrated resort fronting Marina Bay in Singapore and a landmark of the city. At its opening in 2010, it was deemed the world's most expensive standalone casino property at S$8 billion (US$6.88 billion). The resort includes a 1,850-room hotel, a 120,000-square-metre (1,300,000 sq ft) meetings and conventions facility at Sands Expo & Convention Centre, a 74,000-square-metre luxury shopping mall, The Shoppes at Marina Bay Sands, an ArtScience museum, a 2,183-capacity theatre, the world's first floating Apple store, the world's first Louis Vuitton Island Maison, celebrity chef and signature restaurants, and a casino with 500 tables and 3,000 electronic gaming machines. The complex includes three towers topped by the Sands Skypark, a 340-metre-long (1,120 ft) skyway connecting the towers with a capacity of 3,902 people and a 150 m (490 ft) infinity swimming pool, set on top of the world's largest public cantilevered platform, which overhangs the north tower by 66.5 m (218 ft). The 20-hectare resort was designed by Moshe Safdie. The main contractor was Ssangyong Engineering and Construction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Marina_Bay_Sands_%28I%29.jpg/330px-Marina_Bay_Sands_%28I%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marina_Bay_Sands","wikidata":"Q548679"},{"title":"Marina","blocks":[{"text":"A marina is a dock or area of water with piers and moorings for securing and parking yachts and small boats. A marina differs from a port in that a marina is not designed to handle large passenger ships or freighters, and is often for leisure boating activities such as yachting, sailing and boat tours."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Guarda-corpo_da_Avenida_Portugal_-_Rio_de_Janeiro_-_20220923024517.jpg/330px-Guarda-corpo_da_Avenida_Portugal_-_Rio_de_Janeiro_-_20220923024517.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marina","wikidata":"Q721207"},{"title":"Bay","blocks":[{"text":"A bay is a recessed, coastal body of water that directly connects to a larger main body of water, such as an ocean, a lake, or another bay. A large bay is usually called a gulf, sea, sound, or bight. A cove is a small, circular bay with a narrow entrance. A fjord is an elongated bay formed by glacial action.\nThe term embayment is also used for related features, such as extinct bays or freshwater environments."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg/330px-Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay","wikidata":"Q39594"},{"title":"Bay (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Bay is a hair coat color of horses, characterized by a reddish-brown or brown body color with a black point coloration on the mane, tail, ear edges, and lower legs. Bay is one of the most common coat colors in many horse breeds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/BayMare.jpg/330px-BayMare.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay_(horse)","wikidata":"Q900906"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/View_of_MBS_from_the_gardens_%288026531707%29.jpg/500px-View_of_MBS_from_the_gardens_%288026531707%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/View_of_MBS_from_the_gardens_%288026531707%29.jpg/1280px-View_of_MBS_from_the_gardens_%288026531707%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/View_of_MBS_from_the_gardens_%288026531707%29.jpg/500px-View_of_MBS_from_the_gardens_%288026531707%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"View of the three main towers, inspired by decks of cards","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AView_of_MBS_from_the_gardens_(8026531707).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Rooftop_Pool_Marina_bay_Singapore_%2839289149252%29.jpg/500px-Rooftop_Pool_Marina_bay_Singapore_%2839289149252%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Rooftop_Pool_Marina_bay_Singapore_%2839289149252%29.jpg/1280px-Rooftop_Pool_Marina_bay_Singapore_%2839289149252%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Rooftop_Pool_Marina_bay_Singapore_%2839289149252%29.jpg/500px-Rooftop_Pool_Marina_bay_Singapore_%2839289149252%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&